{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Config-driven type mapping + type-granular skip (collapse round-trip via rebar-type label)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nTicket-type mapping is hardcoded (`value_maps.LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`) and whole-type sync\nexclusion is a fixed frozenset (`config.EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`). A Jira project lacking a rebar\ntype has no recourse: it can neither remap the type to an analog (Epic→Initiative) nor cleanly\nskip it. Type must become config-driven on the S1 core with three outcomes — **remap**,\n**skip** (type-granular per-project whole-ticket exclusion), and **fail-closed** on an\nunmapped, non-skipped type. Because rebar may carry more types than a target Jira, a\n**non-injective collapse** must be allowed and made round-trip-safe by a new `rebar-type:`\nannotation label, symmetric with the existing `rebar-status:` machinery.\n\nRound-1 plan-review BLOCKED (6 findings): the seam touches more consumers than the original\n4-file scope. This re-plan enumerates the full, current consumer census (verified at HEAD).\n\n## Approach\n\nWire the S1 `type_map` axis (`mapping_config.MappingLayer.type_map` already exists; `SKIP =\n\"skip\"` sentinel; `validate` already vocab-checks values). Add `config.effective_type_map(\nproject_key, root)` mirroring the existing `config.effective_status_map` (config.py:77):\neffective map = built-in `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>`. A mapped type is\nremapped; a type whose config value is `SKIP` extends per-project exclusion; an unmapped,\nnon-skipped syncable type is a **load-time fail-closed error**, never a silent coerce.\n\n**Fail-closed mechanism (B5/B6).** The syncable local-type universe is derived, not hardcoded:\n`set(typing.get_args(rebar.types.TicketType)) - EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` = {bug, epic, story,\ntask}. `config.effective_type_map` (or a sibling `validate_type_coverage`) asserts every\nsyncable type resolves to a target OR `SKIP`; otherwise it raises the named error at load. The\nthree create paths that today coerce an unknown type to a default (`.get(ticket_type,\"Task\")` /\n`.capitalize()`) are changed to consult the effective map and **surface the error rather than\ncoerce** — removing the silent-drift default that contradicted the ticket's own guarantee.\n\n**Collapse round-trip (B2).** Stamping is OUTBOUND and lives in `outbound_labels.py` (NOT\ninbound_fields, which holds only recovery). Add a `rebar-type:` analog next to the status one:\n`_REBAR_TYPE_LABEL_PREFIX = \"rebar-type:\"`, `_desired_type_annotation`,\n`_diff_type_annotation_labels` (mirror `_desired_status_annotation`:89 /\n`_diff_status_annotation_labels`:114). Invoke the type-stamp diff from `outbound_differ.py`\nat the same site the status stamp is threaded. Inbound recovery adds `recover_type_label` to\n`inbound_fields.py` (mirror `recover_status_label`:152) and prefers it at the type-assignment\nsite (`_map_jira_to_local_fields`, inbound_fields.py:313) before the built-in\n`_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE.get(...)` fallback — inbound stays reverse-map-free, exactly as S2 chose\nfor status.\n\n**Excluded-prefix registration (B3).** `rebar-type:` must be excluded so the annotation label\nis not treated as a user tag (spurious REMOVE mutations). The prefix list consolidated since\nround 1: the canonical tuple is `outbound_labels._EXCLUDED_PREFIXES` (outbound_labels.py:34),\nimported by `outbound_differ` and `inbound_differ` (and read by `reconcile_check` via\n`inbound_differ`). `inbound_translate.py` keeps an INDEPENDENT copy (inbound_translate.py:53-58).\nSo B3 = exactly two edits: add `\"rebar-type:\"` to outbound_labels.py:34 AND to\ninbound_translate.py:58.\n\n**Per-project skip threading (B4).** `outbound_differ.py:377` loads\n`_load_config().EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` (a project-blind frozenset) into\n`_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets`. Thread the ticket's project key so the effective\nexcluded set = `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES ∪ {t : effective_type_map(project)[t] == SKIP}`. Expose\nthis as `config.effective_excluded_types(project_key, root)` so the skip decision is computed\nin one place and consumed by the differ.\n\n**Hierarchy consequence (doc).** Collapsing to a same/lower Jira hierarchy level forfeits the\nparent role; children then fall to the S7 breadcrumb path. Documented, not solved here.\n\n## Surface-parity census (create/remap consumers of the type axis)\n\n- **Outbound create — REST/outbound_fields** (`adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:143`,\n  `_LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE.get(ticket_type,\"Task\")`): IN scope — route through `effective_type_map`;\n  remove the `\"Task\"` default.\n- **Outbound create — Jira DC backend** (`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:86`, same\n  pattern): IN scope — same fix.\n- **Outbound create — ACLI adapter** (`adapters/jira/acli.py:282`,\n  `.get(\"ticket_type\",\"Task\").capitalize()`, a DISTINCT coercion bypassing `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`):\n  IN scope — route through `effective_type_map`; remove the `.capitalize()` default.\n- **Inbound recovery** (`inbound_fields.py:313`): IN scope — `recover_type_label` then built-in\n  inverse.\n- **Dual-direction**: outbound stamp ↔ inbound recover both proven (round-trip test).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `config.py` — `effective_type_map`, `effective_excluded_types`, fail-closed coverage check.\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py`,\n  `adapters/jira/acli.py` — route creates through the effective map; drop silent defaults.\n- `outbound_labels.py` — `rebar-type:` stamp analog + prefix registration (line 34).\n- `outbound_differ.py` — invoke the type stamp; thread per-project skip set.\n- `inbound_fields.py` — `recover_type_label` + prefer it at the type-assignment site.\n- `inbound_translate.py` — register `rebar-type:` in the independent prefix copy (line 58).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_type_mapping.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Config-effect contrast:** `type_map.epic=\"Initiative\"` → an outbound epic targets\n  `Initiative`; default targets the built-in — same path, different config.\n- **Skip (per-project):** a `skip`-mapped type excludes that type's tickets from sync for that\n  project only; another project still syncs it — asserted on the sync decision.\n- **Fail-closed:** an unmapped, non-skipped syncable type raises the named validation error at\n  load; a valid config does not raise. (Asserted through the create path, not just validate.)\n- **Round-trip (collapse):** two distinct rebar types collapsing to one Jira type stamp\n  `rebar-type:` labels; inbound recovers each distinct rebar type. Also assert `rebar-type:`\n  produces no spurious tag REMOVE mutation (B3 regression guard).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `config.effective_type_map` = built-in ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>`; a non-default\n  overlay changes the outbound type through the real create path (all three adapters) —\n  verified by `test_type_mapping.py::test_type_config_effect`.\n- [ ] A `skip`-mapped type excludes that type from sync per-project only, via\n  `config.effective_excluded_types` threaded into `outbound_differ` — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_type_skip_per_project`.\n- [ ] An unmapped, non-skipped syncable type (universe =\n  `get_args(TicketType) - EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`) fails closed at load with a named error; no\n  create path coerces to a silent default — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_unmapped_type_fails_closed`.\n- [ ] Distinct types collapsing to one Jira type round-trip losslessly via `rebar-type:` labels\n  (stamped in `outbound_labels`, registered in both `_EXCLUDED_PREFIXES` copies, recovered in\n  `inbound_fields`), producing no spurious tag mutation — verified by\n  `test_type_mapping.py::test_type_collapse_roundtrip`.\n\nTest tier: **in-process unit** — type resolution, skip decision, fail-closed, and label\nround-trip are pure/observable; oracles are the produced type field, the sync decision, the\nraised error, and the recovered type. Round-1 remediation of all 6 blocking findings (B1–B6)\nis captured in the prior comment; f1bc (outbound_differ split) landed as the size prerequisite."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787352406208823001,"uuid":"f92453e6-6b67-4590-bdda-4af96bc70919"}